  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "RoPE is applied inside self_attn, per block — never here",
      "text": "freqs is one buffer of 1024 rows, split across the head dim as (c − 2·⌊c/3⌋, ⌊c/3⌋, ⌊c/3⌋) for the (f, h, w) axes, then broadcast over the 3D grid. With dim {{cfg.dim}} / {{cfg.num_heads}} heads, c = 64 complex pairs → 22/21/21.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "wan.model",
          "lines": [
            45,
            51
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "rope_apply",
            "first": "def rope_apply(x, grid_sizes, freqs):",
            "sha": "917842d1",
            "span": [
              45,
              72
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Text never gets RoPE and never gets modulated",
      "text": "cross_attn takes norm3(x) as Q and the raw context as K/V. The 6 AdaLN taps only touch the video stream — see e[0..2] on self-attn and e[3..5] on the FFN inside the block.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "wan.model",
          "lines": [
